(1A) A person carrying on an incorporated business may subject to the prior written approval of the Commissioner alter the date to which the accounts of the business are made up.

(1B)  A  person  seeking  the  approval  of  the  Commissioner  under subsection

(1A) shall apply in writing to the Commissioner at least six months before the date to which the accounts are intended to be made up.

(1C)  The  Commissioner  shall  within  six  months  from  the  date  of receipt  of  the  application  communicate  his  decision  in  writing  to  the applicant.

